WEBVTT

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:27.440
Speaker 1: You see, there are some topics that a lot of Christians claim to understand, but every time you interact with them, especially on a deeper level or just watch their manner of life, you know that they don't understand it at all.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:34.000
Speaker 1: And one of those topics is actually the concept of salvation itself.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.360
Speaker 1: What does it mean to be born again?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:54.880
Speaker 1: You see, this is the type of topic that when someone is scrolling social media or YouTube and sees the thumbnail saying, you know, born again, you just scroll past, you've been there, done that, got the T shirt, you already know what it means, but most people don't truly understand it.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:08.140
Speaker 1: And one of the ways I know that people don't understand it is how they treat people who are well behaved and people who are not well behaved, both of whom don't know Jesus.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:18.780
Speaker 1: If you don't see people who don't know Jesus, and no matter how well behaved they are in character, you still have the same urgency for their salvation.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.280
Speaker 1: You don't understand salvation another way I know that people don't really understand salvation.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.240
Speaker 1: Just ask them to preach.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.200
Speaker 1: Ask them to preach.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.440
Speaker 1: Ask them to preach.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:38.800
Speaker 1: You know, there is this proclivity for them to focus on the moral excellence virtue of Christians and not the real essence of salvation.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:46.880
Speaker 1: You know, even as a Christian, and some of you probably bear witness to this, I have been irked by the way some people preach.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.930
Speaker 1: You know, sometimes I had to check myself, like, why?

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.650
Speaker 1: Why does this upset me this much?

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.170
Speaker 1: You know, and all that.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:02:02.650
Speaker 1: Because some people, the way they go about their evangelism is just totally wrong.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.770
Speaker 1: Preaching at people, preaching against people.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:10.370
Speaker 1: Nonetheless, there are things that must be understood when it comes to salvation.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:14.170
Speaker 1: And I wish I could think of a better acronym, but let's just stick to this.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.950
Speaker 1: Well, this is not even an acronym, just key letters that you can use to remember.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.630
Speaker 1: Cndp.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:27.110
Speaker 1: Okay, C for context, N for necessity, D for definition, and P for provision.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:45.920
Speaker 1: And I believe that if you want to really grasp what being born again is about, the moment you understand the context, you understand the necessity, do you understand the definition and the provision, then, at least at the foundational level, you know what it is to know, starting with the context.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:53.356
Speaker 1: You see, when Jesus told Nicodemus, you must be born again, Nicodemus replied in John 3.

00:02:53.444 --> 00:03:04.480
Speaker 1: 4, Look at a man who is alive, a full grown man, and say, be born.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.010
Speaker 1: Are you getting what I'm saying?

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:08.810
Speaker 1: You see?

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:15.370
Speaker 1: So now he goes on, he says, can he enter a second time into his mother's womb and be born?

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:22.170
Speaker 1: And Jesus answered, except you're born of water and the spirit, you cannot enter the kingdom.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.330
Speaker 1: Whoever is born of the flesh is making a distinction.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.650
Speaker 1: Now, the birth they're talking about is biological life.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:32.090
Speaker 1: Whoever is born of the flesh is flesh, but whoever is born of the spirit is spirit.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.360
Speaker 1: So Jesus is saying you actually must be born of the spirit.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:36.600
Speaker 1: So understand this.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.720
Speaker 1: You have biological life.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:44.960
Speaker 1: Every one of us was in our mother's wombs for about nine months on average, okay?

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.080
Speaker 1: And then were born.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.240
Speaker 1: There is an origin to our biological life.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:55.200
Speaker 1: And Jesus is saying there must be an origin to your spiritual life in Christ, okay?

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.880
Speaker 1: Your life in Christ will have no end, but it will have a beginning.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.950
Speaker 1: Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:07.670
Speaker 1: So he's saying, just the same way you were born of the flesh, you must be born of the spirit.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.750
Speaker 1: You must be born of the spirit.

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:13.030
Speaker 1: And there is a contradistinction there.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:22.150
Speaker 1: God created man to coexist in two different worlds and in fact, to operate all right from the spirit realm.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:27.190
Speaker 1: But something fundamentally wrong happened in Genesis chapter three.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.100
Speaker 1: That spiritual part of man died.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:34.820
Speaker 1: And this is why God told Adam, the day you eat of that fruit, you will surely die.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.860
Speaker 1: But guess what?

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:40.660
Speaker 1: When Adam ate of the fruit, he was still walking, he was still talking, but he was dead.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.100
Speaker 1: He was dead.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.740
Speaker 1: Ephesians 2 says you.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:45.860
Speaker 1: Hath he quickened you?

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:46.940
Speaker 1: Hath he made alive?

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:53.460
Speaker 1: Talking to believers who were dead in trespasses and sins, you were dead, and he has made you alive.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.720
Speaker 1: So the same way you have biological life, there is a spiritual life.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.920
Speaker 1: A spiritual life, you see, Just the same way.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.520
Speaker 1: I'll never forget the first burial I attended in my life.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:13.440
Speaker 1: I was still a very young boy, and it was a man I knew very well, very kind man, very generous.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:16.400
Speaker 1: And they told me, he's dead.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.240
Speaker 1: I went to his house for his burial.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.360
Speaker 1: Sure enough, there he was in the coffin.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:28.710
Speaker 1: He still looked pretty much the same, as good as ever, as far as I could recollect as the young boy that I was.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.350
Speaker 1: In fact, he dressed better than usual.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:33.510
Speaker 1: But they said, he's dead.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.910
Speaker 1: For my age, I could have thought he was sleeping, but he's dead.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.670
Speaker 1: He looked the same, but something inside him was missing.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:49.560
Speaker 1: It dawned on me for the first time that the body is just a casing, all right?

00:05:50.360 --> 00:06:06.000
Speaker 1: So spiritual life can be imparted into a person, and it is that part of you, that spiritual part of you that is born again, even though the efficacy transcends beyond your spirit to your soul and even to your body.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:13.760
Speaker 1: Eventually, the next thing I want to Talk about is the necessity for salvation, you see?

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:34.000
Speaker 1: And this one is very important because naturally, if you grew up in a traditional Christian home, when you see people who are smoking and have red eye, maybe are talking to you, maybe who we call Egbo adubus, gangsters, all right?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.080
Speaker 1: So there's every tendency for you to look at a person like that and be overwhelmed with compassion for their souls.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.040
Speaker 1: You want them to be saved immediately, you know, why are you doing this to yourself?

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:44.810
Speaker 1: you need to be saved.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:47.370
Speaker 1: This sinful life will destroy you.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:07:13.770
Speaker 1: But when you see someone who is cool, calm, collected, has a successful business, he's not a churchgoer, he's not religious, but no vices in the person's life per se, maybe he's even more behaved than Christians that, you know, will there be as much incentive for you to see, you know, the futility of the person's efforts and the eventual destiny of the person if the person doesn't place his faith in Jesus?

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:30.110
Speaker 1: All right, so these are the issues, and that's why it is noteworthy that Jesus looked at Nicodemus, a mentor's mentor, a centurion, and a very morally excellent man, at least for the standards of those days, all right?

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:34.590
Speaker 1: And he said, you must be born again.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.070
Speaker 1: You must be born again.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.510
Speaker 1: You are well behaved, boy.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:40.600
Speaker 1: You must be born again, all right?

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.440
Speaker 1: I mean, you've heard it said.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.760
Speaker 1: I really like that saying, just being in a garage doesn't make you a car.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:47.720
Speaker 1: All right?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:50.200
Speaker 1: So you might be going to church and you're not born again.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:57.000
Speaker 1: So when you see the necessity of the gospel preached to people like Cornelius, all right?

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.920
Speaker 1: And preach to Nicodemus, okay?

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:07.350
Speaker 1: Then you now realize that this really isn't about good behavior.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:10.070
Speaker 1: It's about faith in Jesus, okay?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:16.230
Speaker 1: Cornelius had to send for Peter so that you receive words by which you'll be saved.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:19.590
Speaker 1: And Jesus told Nicodemus, you must be born again.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.590
Speaker 1: So bear this in mind, all right?

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.070
Speaker 1: And I've had.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:30.550
Speaker 1: I've explained this earlier in this series how that, listen, being born again is the dead coming back to life.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.688
Speaker 1: And that brings me to the definition D. Right, cndp, all right?

00:08:34.688 --> 00:08:36.289
Speaker 1: It's the dead coming back to life.

00:08:36.448 --> 00:08:41.009
Speaker 1: And some people just think that if you're well behaved, then God should let you into heaven.

00:08:41.249 --> 00:08:43.249
Speaker 1: I mean, it doesn't work that way.

00:08:43.249 --> 00:08:44.369
Speaker 1: Good people die.

00:08:45.329 --> 00:08:46.369
Speaker 1: Good people die.

00:08:47.089 --> 00:08:52.609
Speaker 1: And to be born again is to receive supernatural life, to receive the life of God, all right?

00:08:52.849 --> 00:09:01.089
Speaker 1: That's why the Bible also calls it regeneration, to be translated from a King from the kingdom of darkness into the kingdom of light.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.700
Speaker 1: That takes power, not behavior.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.580
Speaker 1: It takes power.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.220
Speaker 1: Paul said, I'm not ashamed of the gospel of Christ.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:10.500
Speaker 1: It's the power of God unto salvation to those who believe.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:15.700
Speaker 1: See, you may be a churchgoer, you may even be saved and not really know how to articulate and explain this.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.260
Speaker 1: If you go out for evangelism and you ask someone, are you born again?

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:25.300
Speaker 1: And they say, well, I'm a good person and I even behave better than many people in your church, what do you say?

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.070
Speaker 1: You must be able to articulate this clearly.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:28.870
Speaker 1: All right?

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:32.270
Speaker 1: So the same way biological life has an origin.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:36.510
Speaker 1: When you place your faith in Jesus, you receive the life of Christ, okay?

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:44.230
Speaker 1: You receive the Holy Spirit, you know, who dwells in you know, animates your spirit and you become alive to God, okay?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.470
Speaker 1: And that's what it means to be born again.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:52.070
Speaker 1: And next most important point is provision, provision.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:57.570
Speaker 1: You see, the Bible says that if the Lord should count iniquities, who shall stand?

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:58.770
Speaker 1: Alright?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:03.810
Speaker 1: The requirements for salvation, none of us can meet it by works.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:09.970
Speaker 1: So you have to understand this, the very simple text that everybody knows, including Muslims, John 3:16.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:17.290
Speaker 1: For God so loved the world, he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believes in him should not perish but have everlasting life.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.970
Speaker 1: That's God's provision for everlasting life.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:21.700
Speaker 1: That you believe in Jesus.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.260
Speaker 1: You place your faith in Jesus, okay?

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:29.540
Speaker 1: And it is at the point that you place your faith in Jesus that you receive the life of Christ.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:37.380
Speaker 1: When you place your faith in Jesus specifically, that he died for your sins and rose again for your justification.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.380
Speaker 1: You know what Romans 9, 10 says?

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:49.310
Speaker 1: That if you should confess your mouth the Lord Jesus and believe in your heart that God raised him from the dead, you shall be saved with the heart.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.110
Speaker 1: Man believes unto righteousness with the mouth.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.470
Speaker 1: Confession is made unto salvation.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.030
Speaker 1: That's how it works.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:57.150
Speaker 1: You place your faith in Jesus.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:01.550
Speaker 1: And because Jesus took your place and died your death, that provision is enough.

00:11:02.749 --> 00:11:07.470
Speaker 1: And if you don't meet that provision, whatever else you do will not be sufficient.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:11.430
Speaker 1: For there is no other name given under heaven by which men should be saved.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:19.000
Speaker 1: Listen to me, when you understand these foundational principles, whatever else you don't quite get is not as important.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:31.960
Speaker 1: Whether you come out for an altar call or you believe the Gospel just watching the tv, it is at the point of faith and confession that you are saved at that point.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:39.560
Speaker 1: In fact, I've said, you know, strictly speaking that most people get saved before their altar court.

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:39.730
Speaker 1: Because.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:48.760
Speaker 1: Because at the point of the sermon where you believe and understand the message and you just place your trust in Jesus in your heart, that's the point where you are saved.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:49.560
Speaker 1: All right?

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:56.440
Speaker 1: And that's why in Acts 10, the Bible says, while Peter yet speak these words, the Holy Ghost fell on the all them that heard.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:01.640
Speaker 1: You know, that all in Cornelius's house who heard fell.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.320
Speaker 1: Peter was still speaking.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:15.240
Speaker 1: So Peter hadn't even gotten to the point of the sermon where, you see, now if you know, if you are here and you say, brother Peter, I understand what you're saying, and I really believe in Jesus and I want to receive him.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:21.280
Speaker 1: He didn't get to that point at the point where faith was dead in their hearts, the Holy Spirit descended.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:23.959
Speaker 1: And that's really how it works, okay?

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:28.640
Speaker 1: And it's not really about giving your life to Christ.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:34.540
Speaker 1: You can give your life to Christ in consecration, and only when you have first and foremost receive the life of Christ.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:34.930
Speaker 1: Christ.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:39.170
Speaker 1: Salvation is receiving the life of Christ, receiving the Holy Spirit.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.090
Speaker 1: That's what salvation is.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:49.890
Speaker 1: So when you receive Christ's life, then you can give him your life in consecration and in service, because the life that you now live is his.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:50.450
Speaker 1: Right.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:51.730
Speaker 1: Galatians 2:20.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.090
Speaker 1: So that's.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:59.170
Speaker 1: So now these are foundational things that even believers don't know.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:14.280
Speaker 1: And if you're doubting, ask a few people, maybe in your contact list or somebody today, even believers, ask them on some of these things, do you really understand the context or the necessity or the definition or the provision of salvation?

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:16.440
Speaker 1: And you'll be shocked what you will hear.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:22.160
Speaker 1: Listen, just ask people who even evangelize often, what do you say when you're talking to people?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:26.160
Speaker 1: How do you help them understand the message?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.040
Speaker 1: And you'll be shocked.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.630
Speaker 1: And you also don't assume you know it.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.190
Speaker 1: Go through all of this.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.870
Speaker 1: If you need to watch this video again and again, go through it.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:40.030
Speaker 1: You know, a lot of Christians like complicated, sophisticated stuff, Greek words and all of that.

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:43.710
Speaker 1: This one that you consider foundational.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.830
Speaker 1: You can't be effective as a Christian if you don't know this.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.390
Speaker 1: If you can't lead people to Christ, you're not in ministry.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:50.270
Speaker 1: It's that simple.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:53.470
Speaker 1: So I want you to take your time, learn these things.

00:13:55.070 --> 00:14:02.830
Speaker 1: And I can't wait to hear your stories of many more people brought into the kingdom through this teaching.
